From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:50:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] fix: text direction menu stays the three-choice menu when the selection holds inline code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 1.0 (2026-10-16)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0020)

Problem: with a selection that holds some inline code (e.g. a paragraph with
`Shift`), the "Text direction" menu showed only two choices (right-to-left
segment / left-to-right segment, the code menu of patch 0001) and the alignment
menu was hidden. Choosing "right-to-left segment" only wrapped the text in
control characters, so the paragraph went back to its old direction.

Cause: the menus were chosen by "is any part of the selection code".

Fix: the text direction menu (right to left / left to right / automatic) and
the alignment menu are shown whenever the selection is not in a code block.
The two code-segment choices are shown only when the whole selection is code
(inline code or a code block), next to the direction menu.

Files (1; N = new, M = modified, D = deleted):
  M app/editor/menus/formatting.tsx

---
---

diff --git a/app/editor/menus/formatting.tsx b/app/editor/menus/formatting.tsx
index 5abc97a..566be94 100644
